# Public widget requests (no sign-in). The widget iframe runs on our origin, so
# POSTs carry Origin = APP_URL. "host" is the customer's site the widget is shown on.
# Take the bot's publicKey from bots.http; set allowedDomains to limit where it works.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/widget
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@key = PASTE_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE
@visitorId = visitor-local-1
@conversationId = PASTE_CONVERSATION_ID_HERE

### Widget config — also records "last seen on" for the host
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/config?host=https://shop.example.com/pricing

### Ask as a visitor (SSE, same events as the playground; counts toward the monthly limit)
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/chat
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Do you ship to Canada?",
  "visitorId": "{{visitorId}}",
  "host": "shop.example.com"
}

### Follow-up in the same conversation
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/chat
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "And how long does it take?",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "visitorId": "{{visitorId}}",
  "host": "shop.example.com"
}

### Restore the conversation after a page reload
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/conversations/{{conversationId}}?visitorId={{visitorId}}&host=shop.example.com

### Leave an email when the bot couldn't help — 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/lead
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "visitorId": "{{visitorId}}",
  "email": "visitor@example.com",
  "host": "shop.example.com"
}

### Site not in allowedDomains — 403 domain_not_allowed
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{key}}/config?host=https://someone-else.io
